1. What is constructor?
A constructor is a special method used to initialize object data when the object is created..
When we create an object, the constructor is automatically call and give the value of object.
Example: -
class Vehicle {
             Vehicle() {      // Vehicle constructor.
                             System.out.println(“object created”)
 }
    }
2.Types of constructors
They are two type of constructor
1. Default constructor.
2. Userdefined constructor: 2.1 Non Argument constructor. 2.2 Parameterized constructor.
1.What is default constructor?
A constructor automatically added by the compiler when no argument is defined. If programmer not write constructor. Java create own constructor.
Default constructor added only if there is no user-defined constructor inside java file.
2.What is parameterized constructor?
A constructor that accept parameters to initialize object data at creation time.
In short form when the object is creted we pass the value and set the data.

3.Constructor overloading?
Constructor overloading is a technique in object-oriented programming (OOP) where a class has multiple constructors with different parameter lists (number or types of arguments).
4.Difference between constructor and method
Constructor: -
•Name of constructor must be same as the class name.
•Constructor will not have an return statement
•Constructor can not be allow static, final, abstract keywords so, it can never be static, final synchronized.
•A constructor is executed when object is created because constructor is called at time of object creation.
•Method: -
•A method can have any name.
•A method will always have Return statement
.A method can be static final, abstract or synchronized.
.A method is executed when method is called.
5.What is this keyword?
The this keyword in Java refers to the current object in a method or constructor.
The this keyword is often used to avoid confusion when class attributes have the same name as method or constructor parameters

6.What is super keyword?
In Java, the super keyword is used to refer to the parent class of a subclass.
The most common use of the super keyword is to eliminate the confusion between superclasses and subclasses that have methods with the same name.
It can be used in two main ways:
To access attributes and methods from the parent class
To call the parent class constructor

